{"vftra-Gna": [{"id": "vftra-Gna", "headword": "वृत्र-घ्न", "headword_slp1": "vftra-Gna", "fold": "vftra-Gna", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Vṛtra-ghna occurs in a passage of the aitareya brāhmaṇa, where in a gāthā reciting the prowess of bharata it is said that he bound horses on the yamunā (Jumna) and gaṅgā (Ganges) Vṛtraghne, which Sāyaṇa renders ‘at vṛtraghna,’ as the name of a place. Roth, however, seems right in interpreting the form as a dative, ‘for the slayer of Vṛtra’--i.e., indra.\nFoot notes viii. 23, 5.\nSt. Petersburg Dictionary, s.v. Cf. Aufrecht, Aitarecya brāhmaṇa, 425.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["ghna", "vRRitra", "vRRitra-ghna", "vRRitraghna", "vRitra", "vRitra-ghna", "vRitraghna", "vRtra", "vRtra-ghna", "vRtraghna", "vRutra", "vRutra-ghna", "vRutraghna", "vṛtra", "vṛtra-ghna", "vṛtraghna", "घ्न", "वृत्र", "वृत्रघ्न", "ఘ్న", "వృత్ర", "వృత్ర-ఘ్న", "వృత్రఘ్న", "ಘ್ನ", "ವೃತ್ರ", "ವೃತ್ರ-ಘ್ನ", "ವೃತ್ರಘ್ನ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ghna", "vRRitra", "vRRitra-ghna", "vRRitraghna", "vRitra", "vRitra-ghna", "vRitraghna", "vRtra", "vRtra-ghna", "vRtraghna", "vRutra", "vRutra-ghna", "vRutraghna", "vṛtra", "vṛtra-ghna", "vṛtraghna", "Gna", "vftra", "vftraGna", "ఘ్న", "వృత్ర", "వృత్ర-ఘ్న", "వృత్రఘ్న", "ಘ್ನ", "ವೃತ್ರ", "ವೃತ್ರ-ಘ್ನ", "ವೃತ್ರಘ್ನ"]}], "vftra-sanku": [{"id": "vftra-SaMku", "headword": "वृत्र-शंकु", "headword_slp1": "vftra-SaMku", "fold": "vftra-sanku", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Vṛtra-śaṅku, literally ‘Vṛtra-peg,’ found in one passage of the Śatapatha brāhmaṇa, is said by the scholiast on the Kātyāyana śrauta sūtra to denote a stone pillar. This improbable interpretation is based on another passage in the same brāhmaṇa.\nFoot notes xiii. 8, 4, 1.\nxxi. 3, 31.\niv. 2, 5, 15. Cf. Eggeling. Sacred Books of the East, 44, 437, n. 1.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["shaMku", "shanku", "vRRitra", "vRRitra-shaMku", "vRRitra